|* ro_ring5 transient-noise jitter accumulation -- issue #10 flagship config
|*
|* Purpose: issue #10 acceptance criterion 2. Measures period T0 (`tbar`)
|* and jitter accumulation sigma_1/sigma_2/sigma_4/sigma_8 (`sigma_N`) for
|* design/ro_ring5.spice's 5-stage starved ring (1 ro_nand2 enable/stop
|* stage + 4 ro_stage delay cells -- design/README.md's "the cheap
|* transient-noise vehicle for the jitter characterization", explicitly
|* named in design/xschem/ for exactly this purpose), across the sky130
|* PVT grid.
|*
|* This is the campaign's FULL 27-point-grid flagship configuration (the
|* full {tt,ss,ff} x {-40,27,125 degC} x {nominal +/-10% supply} grid, per
|* spec/porting-plan.md Sec 3.1/DR-0006-style reduced-grid convention).
|* design/ro_ring11.sch (the actual 11-stage array ring) is the more
|* expensive config and is only run at the 3 PVT headline points -- see
|* tb_ro_ring11_jitter.spice's own header for why, and this ring's own
|* wall-clock-cost re-measurement below.
|*
|* Method (adapted from gf180-trng's sim/tb/ro-inv-05stage-jitter/, cited by
|* spec/porting-plan.md Sec 3.2 as "device-physics testbenches (re-run on
|* sky130 devices, not ported as evidence)"): ngspice's own .tran analysis
|* does not include intrinsic BSIM4 device noise (this is a general ngspice
|* architecture fact, not a PDK-specific one -- confirmed against this
|* checkout's own ngspice build during this campaign's development: a
|* purely deterministic .tran of this same ring, no injected sources at
|* all, converges to a bit-exact repeating period with zero run-to-run
|* seed sensitivity). So every stage's input carries an explicit trnoise()
|* voltage source, in series, exactly mirroring gf180-trng's per-stage
|* injection topology (ro -> gA -> nand2 -> n1 -> gB -> stage1 -> n2 -> ...
|* -> n4 -> gE -> stage4 -> ro).
|*
|* trnoise() calibration: NA=2.0e-3 (V rms), NT=2e-10 (s) -> one-sided
|* injected PSD S_inj = 2*NA^2*NT = 1.6e-15 V^2/Hz (4.0e-08 V/sqrt(Hz)),
|* anchored to sim/ro-stage-noise-mechanism-check/records/
|* 20260825-022446-d58d709.md's own measured onoise_spectrum density near
|* 1 GHz (~4.0e-08 V/sqrt(Hz) at tt, the closest sampled frequency to this
|* ring's own oscillation band) -- the same "anchor the fixed injection
|* level to the device's own measured near-oscillation-band noise density"
|* method gf180-trng's characterization-ro-delay-cell-jitter.md documents
|* (see its "Device .noise cross-check" section), simplified here to a
|* single anchor point rather than a full new per-corner device-.noise
|* sweep (out of this issue's budget -- see this record's caveats).
|* NT=2e-10 gives an implied noise bandwidth (~1/(2*NT) = 2.5 GHz) safely
|* above every oscillation frequency measured in this campaign's own grid.
|* CAVEAT: this is a single fixed injection level, not re-measured per
|* corner -- treat every sigma_N figure below as good to a factor of
|* roughly 1.5-2x, per gf180-trng's own precedent for the same method
|* (its characterization-ro-delay-cell-jitter.md's "Safe to size against"
|* item 5).
|*
|* Wall-clock cost, re-measured for sky130 (spec/porting-plan.md Sec 2.2
|* explicitly asks for this re-measurement rather than assuming gf180-trng's
|* own ~130-150s/run figure ports). Measured on this campaign's development
|* machine (8-core x86-64, ngspice-46, sky130A c6d73a35):
|*
|*   - ~1.9 s of wall clock per simulated ns for this 5-stage ring at
|*     `.tran 5p`, i.e. ~215 s per corner point at this deck's 115 ns tstop.
|*   - That cost is set by the transient step count, NOT by trnoise(): the
|*     same ring, same tstop, same max step, with the trnoise() sources
|*     replaced by plain `dc 0` sources, measured within a few percent of
|*     the same wall clock. (An earlier draft of this header asserted a
|*     ~475x trnoise penalty at NT=1e-11; that figure did not survive
|*     re-measurement at NT=2e-10 and has been struck.)
|*   - ro_ring11 is ~2.2x the devices AND ~2.2x the period, so it costs
|*     ~5x per measured period. That is why THIS ring, not ro_ring11, is
|*     the full-27-point-grid flagship and ro_ring11 runs only the 3
|*     headline points -- exactly the DR-0006 cost/coverage trade-off,
|*     re-measured on sky130 rather than inherited.
|*
|* tstop = 115 ns is sized from a deterministic (noise-free) period probe
|* run over the grid's extremes before this deck was fixed: the slowest
|* corner measured is 4.82 ns/period (ss / -40 degC / 1.62 V; the low-supply
|* edge dominates -- ss/1.98 V runs 2.02 ns/period, a 2.4x supply swing,
|* while -40 -> +125 degC at fixed supply moves it under 2%). 21 rising
|* crossings therefore need <= 5 + 20 x 4.82 = 101 ns, and 115 ns carries
|* the margin. A single uniform tstop across all 27 points (rather than a
|* per-corner one) keeps every record's measurement window identical.
|*
|* 20 periods measured (21 rising crossings, rise=2..22; the first rising
|* edge is discarded as `.ic` startup transient, per gf180-trng's own
|* convention), NOT gf180-trng's 128 -- a budget-driven reduction, made
|* deliberately per spec/porting-plan.md Sec 2.2's prompt to re-measure
|* DR-0006's cost/coverage trade-off rather than copy it: 128 periods at
|* this ring's worst-corner 4.82 ns period would need a ~620 ns tstop, ~20
|* min per corner point, ~9 h for the 27-point grid alone. CAVEAT: with 20
|* period samples the sigma_1 estimator itself carries ~16% (1-sigma)
|* statistical error, hence ~32% on sigma_1^2 and therefore on Q -- that is
|* the resolution floor for any corner-to-corner Q comparison read off this
|* grid, and the reduction in sim/ro-array-sizing/ states it as such.
|* sigma_1/sigma_2/sigma_4/sigma_8 only (no sigma_16/sigma_32 --
|* gf180-trng's own accumulated-jitter figures at N>=16 were themselves
|* flagged as "not yet resolvable trends" even at their much larger
|* period/seed count). CAVEAT: single seed per PVT point (gf180-trng used
|* >=4) -- seed-to-seed spread is NOT characterized by this campaign; a
|* documented gap, not a silent omission. The seed is deliberately held
|* CONSTANT across every point of the grid (common random numbers), so
|* corner-to-corner Q differences are not additionally confounded by
|* seed-to-seed variation.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ss (process axis), /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-10/design/ro_ring5.spice (unused by this file -- the ring
|* is built in place from ro_nand2/ro_stage, both defined by
|* design/ro_ring5.spice, which /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-10/design/ro_ring5.spice still names, so --ro-ring5's
|* default is exactly the file this deck needs .include'd), -40.0/1.98
|* (the other two PVT axes) and 1 (this run's `.option seed=`). As
|* committed here this is not a runnable deck.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ss
|
|.include "/home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-10/design/ro_ring5.spice"
|
|.temp -40.0
|.option seed=1
|
|Vddr vddr 0 dc 1.98
|Ven en 0 dc 1.98
|
|xg gA en n1 vddr 0 ro_nand2
|VnA gA ro dc 0 trnoise(2.0e-3 2e-10 0 0)
|x1 gB n2 vddr 0 ro_stage
|VnB gB n1 dc 0 trnoise(2.0e-3 2e-10 0 0)
|x2 gC n3 vddr 0 ro_stage
|VnC gC n2 dc 0 trnoise(2.0e-3 2e-10 0 0)
|x3 gD n4 vddr 0 ro_stage
|VnD gD n3 dc 0 trnoise(2.0e-3 2e-10 0 0)
|x4 gE ro vddr 0 ro_stage
|VnE gE n4 dc 0 trnoise(2.0e-3 2e-10 0 0)
|
|.ic v(ro)=0 v(n1)=1.98 v(n2)=0 v(n3)=1.98 v(n4)=0
|
|.tran 20p 115n uic
|
|.control
|run
|meas tran vmax_ss MAX v(ro) from=20n to=115n
|meas tran vmin_ss MIN v(ro) from=20n to=115n
|let swing_frac = (vmax_ss - vmin_ss) / 1.98
|let k = 2
|let tc = vector(21)
|while k <= 22
|  meas tran tk when v(ro)=0.5*1.98 rise=$&k
|  let tc[k-2] = tk
|  let k = k + 1
|end
|let tbar = (tc[20] - tc[0])/20
|let r1 = (tc[1,20] - tc[0,19]) - 1*tbar
|let r2 = (tc[2,20] - tc[0,18]) - 2*tbar
|let r4 = (tc[4,20] - tc[0,16]) - 4*tbar
|let r8 = (tc[8,20] - tc[0,12]) - 8*tbar
|let sigma_1 = sqrt(mean(r1*r1)/(1 - 1/20))
|let sigma_2 = sqrt(mean(r2*r2)/(1 - 2/20))
|let sigma_4 = sqrt(mean(r4*r4)/(1 - 4/20))
|let sigma_8 = sqrt(mean(r8*r8)/(1 - 8/20))
|print vmax_ss
|print vmin_ss
|print swing_frac
|print tbar
|print sigma_1
|print sigma_2
|print sigma_4
|print sigma_8
|.endc
|.end
|

